					With Vectis Mail you own the IP, which means 2–4 weeks of gradual IP warmup
					before you have an equivalent reputation. If deliverability on day one matters
					more than long-term cost flatlining or data sovereignty, Postmark is the right
					call.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="alt-faq-q">
				<h3>Why would I stay on Postmark?</h3>
				<p>
					Six honest reasons: (1) you genuinely love the product and the cost feels
					reasonable for your volume; (2) Message Streams is load-bearing for your
					business; (3) you need pre-warmed IPs from day one with no warmup window;
					(4) SOC 2 / HIPAA off-the-shelf is a procurement requirement; (5) you have
					zero sysadmin capacity and want zero infrastructure to think about; (6) you're
					under the cost-crossover line where managed-SaaS economics work for you. If
					none of those apply, the self-host story compounds fast.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

